Zoekt is a fast text search engine intended for source code. It builds
a trigram index and supports substring and regular expression matches,
boolean queries, and filters on file name, repository, language and
branch. When universal-ctags is installed, symbol definitions are
recorded too, so they can be searched with sym: and used for ranking.

The port installs the indexers (zoekt-index for plain directories,
zoekt-git-index and zoekt-local-sync for git repositories, plus the
mirroring helpers), the zoekt command-line search tool, and
zoekt-webserver, which serves a web interface and JSON/gRPC search APIs.
